    <h2>4. 5 Most Confusing Pairs - Do Not Mix Them</h2>
    <table>
      <tr><th>Pair</th><th>First One</th><th>Second One</th></tr>
      <tr><td>== vs ===</td><td>== checks value only - 5 == "5" is true</td><td>=== checks value + type - 5 === "5" is false - Always use ===</td></tr>
      <tr><td>= vs == vs ===</td><td>= is assign - let x = 5</td><td>== / === is compare - Is x equal to 5?</td></tr>
      <tr><td>innerText vs innerHTML</td><td>innerText = Plain text only</td><td>innerHTML = Text + HTML tags - Can add &lt;b&gt;, &lt;div&gt;</td></tr>
      <tr><td>setTimeout vs setInterval</td><td>setTimeout = Once after delay</td><td>setInterval = Again and again</td></tr>
      <tr><td>LocalStorage vs API</td><td>LocalStorage = In browser, no internet</td><td>API = On server, needs internet, live data</td></tr>
    </table>
    <h2>5. Complete Example - All Concepts in One Mini App</h2>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="comment" style="color:#94a3b8">// Counter App - Variables, DOM, Events, Functions, If-Else, LocalStorage, Timers</span><br>
<span class="text">let count = Number(localStorage.getItem("count")) || 0; // Variables + LocalStorage</span><br>
<span class="text">document.getElementById("num").innerText = count; // DOM</span><br><br>
<span class="text">function add() { // Function + Event</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">count++; // Operator</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">if (count === 10) { alert("You reached 10!"); } // If-Else</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">document.getElementById("num").innerText = count; // DOM Update</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text">localStorage.setItem("count", count); // Save</span><br>
<span class="text">}</span><br><br>
<span class="comment" style="color:#94a3b8">// Auto +1 every 5 seconds - Timer</span><br>
<span class="text">setInterval(add, 5000);</span>
    </code></div>
    <h2>6. 5 Challenges - Do Without Looking</h2>
    <p>In Playground, build these in 30 minutes. If you can do all 5, you are ready:</p>
    <p>1. <b>Even / Odd Checker</b> - Input number, button says Even or Odd - Uses if-else + %<br>2. <b>Multiplication Table</b> - Input number, show table 1 to 10 - Uses for loop<br>3. <b>Name List</b> - Input + Add button, names show in list, delete button for each - Uses array + push + splice<br>4. <b>Age Calculator</b> - Input birth year, show age - Uses new Date().getFullYear()<br>5. <b>Random Quote</b> - Button shows random quote from array - Uses Math.random + Math.floor</p>
    <div class="box"><b>Remember:</b> JavaScript = Variables + Logic + DOM | Variables hold data | If-Else makes decisions | Loops repeat | Functions reuse code | Arrays hold list | Objects hold details | DOM changes page | Events respond to user | LocalStorage saves | Timers delay/repeat | API gets live data | Project = Data First, then showTasks(), then save, then events</div>
